From: Stoicoci Mihaita <stoicocimihaita@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] q706f: pm8150b charger: input current limit per source, battery temperature protection

Input current limit
  A wall charger on an A-to-C cable (APSD result DCP/OCP, Type-C Rp
  default) charged with only 900 mA. For Rp-default TCPM asks
  qcom_pmic_typec for the limit, which returns this charger's own
  CURRENT_MAX (900 mA right after attach); the charger then took
  min(DCP limit, TCPM CURRENT_MAX) and so latched its own start value.
  Nothing re-evaluated the limit when TCPM changed either.
  - PD contract: min(contract current, 3 A), from the TCPM supplier.
  - Otherwise Type-C Rp read from the PMIC (TYPE_C_SNK_STATUS): 3 A / 1.5 A.
  - Rp default: BC1.2 (APSD): SDP 500 mA, CDP 1.5 A, DCP/QC 2 A,
    proprietary (OCP) 1.5 A, floating data lines 500 mA.
  - 500 mA while APSD runs and after unplug.
  - Re-evaluate on supplier changes (external_power_changed).
  - Vendor SW_OVERRIDE_HC_MODE (ICL_OVERRIDE_AFTER_APSD) so that
    USBIN_CURRENT_LIMIT_CFG is what applies; AICL stays enabled.

Battery temperature
  New: the temperature of the battery this charger supplies (the gauge
  power supply, as the vendor kernel does) is polled every 10 s while a
  source is attached. Window from the battery node, vendor values
  (lenovo-jeita.c, "P12_battery" profile) as fallback:
    < 0 degC or > 50 degC   charging disabled (health Cold / Overheat)
    <= 15 degC              charge current 1.5 A (Cool)
    > 45 degC               float voltage 4.2 V (Warm)
    no temperature / asleep 1.5 A and 4.2 V
  2 degC hysteresis when leaving a zone; three failed reads are
  tolerated. Suspend and shutdown leave the restricted limits (or
  charging off when already cold/hot) because the PMIC keeps charging
  with nothing watching. The PMIC hardware JEITA stays as it was.

Status and measurements
  - STATUS used the PMI8998 state encoding and an "inhibit" bit that
    does not exist on PM8150B: a charging battery read "Not charging".
  - CURRENT_NOW is the USB input current: the ADC channel gives uV at
    0.2 V/A, so multiply by 5 (it read 176 mA at 900 mA). VOLTAGE_NOW
    (VBUS) and CURRENT_NOW no longer read 0 whenever STATUS is not
    "Charging".
  - HEALTH reports battery over-voltage instead of logging an error on
    every read.
  - CONSTANT_CHARGE_CURRENT / CONSTANT_CHARGE_VOLTAGE show the limits
    in force (read-only).

Termination and recharge
  Programmed from charge-term-current-microamp and
  re-charge-voltage-microvolt when present; DTS: the vendor values for
  this cell at a 4.25 V float voltage (1.7 A, 4.10 V).

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts
index 53c8c038a092a65c6c023418072f79d1f20c4b5d..5d045f19e00dba777a381b8fbaca6e35588d1e5b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts
@@ -84,6 +84,27 @@ battery: battery {
 		 * mitigation level.
 		 */
 		constant-charge-current-max-microamp = <3000000>;
+		/*
+		 * Vendor qcom,chg-term-current-ma = <(-1700)>: charging ends
+		 * once the cell is at the float voltage and takes less than
+		 * 1.7 A (the bq27541 flags "full" on about the same condition).
+		 * Without the charge pumps the cell rarely takes more than
+		 * that, so charging ends soon after the float voltage is
+		 * reached; lower this for a longer constant-voltage phase.
+		 */
+		charge-term-current-microamp = <1700000>;
+		/*
+		 * Vendor recharge threshold for a 4.25 V float voltage
+		 * (EXFG_STEP3_RECHARGE_VOLTAGE_MV); 4.38 V goes with 4.49 V.
+		 */
+		re-charge-voltage-microvolt = <4100000>;
+		/*
+		 * Vendor qcom,jeita-fcc-ranges / qcom,jeita-fv-ranges of the
+		 * "P12_battery" profile: no charging outside 0-50 degC, less
+		 * current up to 15 degC, 4.2 V float above 45 degC.
+		 */
+		operating-range-celsius = <0 50>;
+		alert-celsius = <15 45>;
 	};
 
 	gpio-hall-sensor {
